WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.850
- [Announcer] Principles for Success.

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:05.420
An ultra mini-series
adventure in 30 minutes

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.230
and in eight episodes.

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:11.743
Episode Two, Embrace
Reality and Deal With It.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:17.100
- The path you take in life is
your most important decision.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.990
In my case, I wanted my life to be great

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.370
and I feared boredom and mediocrity

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.560
more than I feared failure.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.580
Since I didn't start out with money,

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:29.130
and I didn't need much
more than a bed to sleep in

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.810
and food to eat, I could skew my decisions

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:33.770
to pursue my adventures.

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:36.980
So ever since I was a kid,
I ran after the things

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.270
I wanted, crashed, got up and ran again,

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:42.880
and crashed again.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:47.190
And each time I crashed I
learned something, got better,

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.000
and crashed less.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.280
By doing that over and over again,

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.500
I learned to love this process,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.770
even the crashing part of it.

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:58.960
Through it, I encountered reality,

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.180
and I learned how to deal with it,

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:05.130
which inspired another one of
my most fundamental principles

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:08.890
which is that truth is
the essential foundation

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:11.550
for producing good outcomes.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:14.190
By truth, I don't mean anything more than

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:16.080
the way the world works.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:20.380
I believe that we were given
the laws of reality by nature.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:23.310
Humans didn't create
them, but we can use them

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:26.980
to foster our own evolution
and achieve our goals.

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:30.320
Realizing that made me a hyperrealist,

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:33.710
by which I mean I became
someone who has discovered

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:37.680
the great rewards of deeply
understanding, accepting,

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.820
and working with reality as it is

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:43.133
and not as I wish it would be.

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:48.080
When I say I'm a hyperrealist,
people sometimes think

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:50.820
I'm saying that dreams can't come true.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.210
That's absolutely not true.

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:57.080
Without pursuing dreams, life is mundane.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:01.210
What I mean is that to me,
hyperrealism is the best way

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:04.150
to choose one's dreams
and then achieve them.

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:09.150
Having big dreams plus
embracing reality plus having

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:13.200
lots of determination will
bring you a successful life.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.730
I believe this formula
is true for everyone,

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:19.400
but what does a successful life look like?

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:23.220
We each have to decide for
ourselves what success is.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:26.300
I don't care whether you want
to be a master of the universe

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:29.440
or to live under a palm
tree or anything else.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:30.453
I really don't.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:35.680
Each of us chooses goals based
on our values and decides

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:40.020
on the best path to achieve
them, but we all need approaches

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:43.820
to making decisions that work
well, especially when facing

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:47.920
problems, mistakes, and
weaknesses that stand in our way.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:51.280
To succeed, we must
embrace all our realities,

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.340
especially the harsh realities
that we wish weren't true.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:58.040
At first, looking at these
harsh realities caused me

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:01.240
a lot of pain, but I learned
that this pain was just

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:05.090
psychological and that by
seeing things differently made

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:06.770
all the difference.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:10.280
I came to view problems like
puzzles that would reward me

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:11.780
if I could solve them.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:14.430
They would help me deal
with the problem at hand,

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:16.900
and they would give me
principles for dealing

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:19.780
with similar problems in the future.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:23.810
I learned to treat pain as
a cue that a great learning

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:27.291
opportunity is at hand,
which led me to realize

00:03:27.291 --> 00:03:32.291
that pain plus reflection equals progress.

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.880
Meditation has been invaluable

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:37.460
in helping me see things that way.

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:40.030
I found that when I calmed myself down

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:43.700
and embraced my realities
and dealt with them,

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:47.930
the rewards brought me
pleasure and the pain faded.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:51.850
Each of us has the unique
capability to think logically

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:54.780
to reflect on ourselves
and our circumstances

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:58.000
and to direct our own personal evolution.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.220
Doing this well is just
a matter of following

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:03.740
a simple five-step process.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:07.860
In episode three, we'll
explore what that process is

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:08.813
and how to use it.

00:04:09.754 --> 00:04:12.587
(words whooshing)

